      <div id="troubleshooting" class="mt-20 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-3xl p-8 lg:p-12 scroll-mt-24">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-black mb-6">Solo Shaving Troubleshooting: How to Fix Common Issues</h3>
        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#FF4500] mb-2">Issue: Missing the "Lower Middle" Spot</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Fix:</strong> Most guys reach over their shoulder for the whole back. For the lower middle, reach <em>under</em> your arm or from the side. The Mangroomer's 135-degree pivot is specifically designed for this "side-reach" maneuver.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#FF4500] mb-2">Issue: Razor Bumps Near the Spine</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Fix:</strong> The skin along the spine is thinner and more sensitive. Use zero pressure here. If using a manual shaver, switch to a "Mild" setting or use a foil shaver (Mangroomer/Philips) for this specific strip.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#FF4500] mb-2">Issue: Hair Tugging/Snagging</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Fix:</strong> Your hair is likely too long or the blades are dull. Use a trimmer first. If using the Mangroomer, engage the "Power Burst" mode. For manual shavers, check if hair is caught between the blades and rinse frequently.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-[#FF4500] mb-2">Issue: Can't See What I'm Doing</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Fix:</strong> Use a "Door Mirror" setup. Hang a three-way mirror on your bathroom door. This provides a 360-degree view of your back, allowing you to use both hands for the shaver rather than holding a hand mirror.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
