        <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-3 text-center">*Laser results are long-lasting but rarely 100% permanent; touch-ups typically needed every 1-2 years</p>

        <div class="mt-8 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
          <h3 class="font-black text-gray-900 mb-3">The Bottom Line on Alternatives</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            For most men, a dedicated back shaver is the clear winner: one-time cost, zero pain, completely solo operation, and results that last long enough for practical maintenance. Laser hair removal is the only method that beats shaving for convenience long-term, but the upfront cost ($1,000–3,000+ for a full course) is prohibitive for most. Depilatory creams like Nair work on the back but are difficult to apply solo and can cause chemical burns on sensitive skin. Professional waxing produces excellent smoothness but at $30-80 every 4-6 weeks, you'll spend over $500/year — far more than any shaver on this list.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

